  "data": {
    "body": "You pull the axel of a pair rolling wheels, mass \\textbf{M} through a distance \\textbf{d} with constant horizontal force of magnitude \\textbf{F}. Next, you pull a block of ice of the same mass on a \\textbf{frictionless} surface through the same distance, applying the same force.\n\nIf both objects start from rest, how will their \\textbf{final translational kinetic energies} compare?",
    "solution": [
      3
    ],
